# The files app's scripted session (examples/odin/files against ref/src/bin/files.rs, gates/pixels.sh
# files): every image must be byte-identical between the two. Offscreen the platform is not asked: the
# `answer` lines answer the app's file dialogs and its prompt (the library's scripted platform for the
# Odin app, the twin's own queue for Rust). The clock moves only on `advance`, so the status line's
# entrance animation is shot at fixed times.
size 720 480
frame
advance 300
frame
shot 01-start.png
# the kit's AppMenuBar: the File menu
click 24 18
frame
shot 02-file-menu.png
# its first item, Open…: the file dialog, answered by the script
click 40 46
frame
shot 03-open-asked.png
answer paths ../../../../files.sample.txt
# the answer's DONE turn runs before the frame that follows it (the `answer` line's own frame), so
# what its handler changed is in that frame, as in Rust (PROTOCOLS.md 11.32)
shot 04-answered.png
advance 100
frame
shot 05-opened-entering.png
advance 300
frame
shot 06-opened.png
# File > Save as…: a save dialog, answered with a file in the app's folder (it writes the text there)
click 17 16
frame
click 40 77
frame
answer new-path saved.txt
advance 400
frame
shot 07-saved.png
# File > Quit: the window's prompt, answered with its second button (Stay)
click 17 16
frame
click 40 113
frame
answer prompt 1
advance 400
frame
shot 08-still-here.png
# Help > Website: open_url (recorded offscreen, not opened)
click 60 16
frame
shot 09-help-menu.png
click 80 49
frame
advance 400
frame
shot 10-website.png
# ctrl-o: the same action by its key binding; the dialog dismissed
key ctrl-o
frame
answer cancel paths
advance 400
frame
shot 11-open-cancelled.png
